[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mComplete Guest VM Outbound Networking\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Networking activates by default for local Firecracker VMs \u2014 `port cluster up` produces a VM with working egress without requiring explicit `[network]` config. (\u001b[2mVFTZdamHM\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Guest `ip addr` shows eth0 with an IP, `ip route` shows a default route via the TAP gateway. (\u001b[2m`kubectl run --rm -it test --image=busybox -- nslookup github.com` succeeds\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-03\u001b[0m - DNS defaults are complete \u2014 even a bare `[machines.demo.network]` section (or no section at all) gets working nameservers. (\u001b[2mCoreDNS resolves external hostnames through the full chain\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFTZdamHM\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Default-On Guest Networking Activation (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-31T12:56:28\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFTZVF3wa/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Complete Guest VM Outbound Networking - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nThe previous networking implementation (VFSRShGlI) added all the structural code \u2014 TAP setup, NAT rules, Firecracker `network_interfaces`, guest init eth0 bring-up \u2014 but gated it behind `Option<MachineNetworkSpec>`. When the TOML config lacks an explicit `[machines.demo.network]` section, `machine.network` is `None` and all networking code is skipped. The guest boots with only loopback, the K3s dummy `port0`, and `cni0` \u2014 no eth0, no default route, no egress. DNS is configured in `/etc/resolv.conf` but packets are unreachable.\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Networking activates by default for local Firecracker VMs \u2014 `port cluster up` produces a VM with working egress without requiring explicit `[network]` config. | board: VFTZdamHM |\r\n| MG-02 | Guest `ip addr` shows eth0 with an IP, `ip route` shows a default route via the TAP gateway. | manual: `kubectl run --rm -it test --image=busybox -- nslookup github.com` succeeds |\r\n| MG-03 | DNS defaults are complete \u2014 even a bare `[machines.demo.network]` section (or no section at all) gets working nameservers. | manual: CoreDNS resolves external hostnames through the full chain |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Minimal change \u2014 fix the activation path, do not redesign the networking stack.\r\n- Backward compatible \u2014 explicit `[machines.demo.network]` configs continue to work.\r\n- Operators can still disable networking with `enabled = false`.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while local Firecracker VMs still boot without a default route.\r\n- HALT when `port cluster up` with no `[network]` section produces a VM where `ping 8.8.8.8` succeeds.\r\n- YIELD if the fix requires changes to the guest image build pipeline beyond what Port controls.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFTZdamHM\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mDefault-On Guest Networking Activation\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-31 12:45:03\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-31 12:51:34\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-31 12:56:19\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-31 12:56:18\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m4m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFTZdamHM/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFTZdamHM/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  MachineSpec.network is Option with no Default \u2014 when TOML lacks [machines.demo.network], all networking code is skipped. Guest boots without eth0, default route, or egress. The dns_servers field also defaults to an empty vec, so even a bare [network] section gets no DNS.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Local Firecracker VMs get networking by default without requiring explicit config. (\u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport cluster up\u001b[0m with no \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61m[network]\u001b[0m section produces a VM with working egress -> \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mping 8.8.8.8\u001b[0m succeeds inside the guest)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - When \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mMachineSpec.network\u001b[0m is \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mNone\u001b[0m, the runtime must use default networking config (enabled=true, 172.16.0.0/24 subnet, DNS 8.8.8.8/8.8.4.4) for local Firecracker VMs.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFTarG3Jq\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Explicit \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61m[machines.*.network]\u001b[0m configs must continue to work unchanged. Operators can disable networking with \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61menabled = false\u001b[0m.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFTarG3Jq\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - Default activation: \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcargo test\u001b[0m passes including config round-trip tests\r\n    - Egress: \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport cluster up\u001b[0m \u2192 guest can reach external hosts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 0 | manual 2\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 0 | manual 2\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 0 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFTarG3Jq\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Default-On Networking Activation Fix (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
